      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Great post. Totally agree that the scaling cap, animation restrictions, and overall limitations this most recent update introduced are odd considering they remove functionality rather than encourage/enhance it. \n\nVRChat is fundamentally built around user expression and as mentioned in the original post this update removes more than it adds.  Previously, players could stage large scale monster battles in pre-existing city worlds. Now it’s impossible without remaking/updating the world. \n\nThe dilemma is obvious, not every giant monster enjoyer has the time or capability to remake their favorite worlds from scratch. Furthermore it’s unlikely that original world authors will remake/rescale their maps considering they’re even active on VRC anymore. So what’s the giant monster enjoyer to do? Their rampage days are effectively gone due to the restrictions of this update. So cmon VRC team, are we really saying goodbye to our rampaging fun? \n\nThis is an opportunity for the developers to align VRC’s functionality with their goal of making VRC THE platform for everyone and THE platform for limitless (not limited) creativity.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
